description:
Along with `Set`s, TypeScript allows for somthing called `Map`s. Maps are Key-Value pairs. Map keys are unique, meaning that if a key already exists, its value is replaced instead of a duplicate being created. Maps have some methods: 2 important ones are `delete(key: <KeyType>): void`, and `set(key: <KeyType>, value: <ValueType>): void`. You create a map with `new Map<KeyType, ValueType>();`. You can technically create a map from any iterable, but most of the time you can only do it with a array of arrays, ([[key, value]]), or another map.

---
## Example 1: Set and Get.
```ts
const contacts = new Map<string, string>();
contacts.set("123-456-7890", "Steve");
contacts.set("132-293-1234", "Paul America");
contacts.set("9988-123-7233", "⹔Ⅸ⽩ɳ⨠⥴ᩥ⑸⩴൮ᱲ⩥ॡቤᱡᡢ⭬եമภ⁈ਠ٭ᱯݪ୩≢ᡡၫ⩥⤮⑲づᅡᩤ⵩᭮ⅧⰠᡴ२ᱩ⥳Ȯ୳");
console.log(contacts);
// Map { "123-456-7890" => "Steve", "132-293-1234" => "Paul America", "9988-123-7233" => "⹔Ⅸ⽩ɳ⨠⥴ᩥ⑸⩴൮ᱲ⩥ॡቤᱡᡢ⭬եമภ⁈ਠ٭ᱯݪ୩≢ᡡၫ⩥⤮⑲づᅡᩤ⵩᭮ⅧⰠᡴ२ᱩ⥳Ȯ୳" }

contacts.delete("9988-123-7233");
contacts.set("123-456-7890", "Steve Broke");
console.log(contacts);
// Map { "123-456-7890" => "Steve", "132-293-1234" => "Paul America" }
```
## Example 2: Map construction.
```ts
const originalMap = new Map();
originalMap.set("1", "2");
const mapCopy = new Map(originalMap);
console.log(mapCopy);
// Map { "1" => "2" }
```

---
# Assignment:
MeTube wants a channel to subscribers registry! Create the addChannel function, which should take a name string subscribers number and channels map, and return the map with an additional pair added, the arguments. DO NOT MODIFY THE ORIGINAL MAP.

runHarness:
let _pass = 0;
let _fail = 0;

function _test(num: number, got: any, expected: any) {
  const passed = got === expected;
  console.log('---------------------');
  console.log('Test ' + num + ':');
  console.log('Output: ' + got);
  console.log(passed ? 'Pass' : 'Fail');
  if (passed) _pass++; else _fail++;
}

const m1 = new Map<string, number>();
const r1 = addChannel("music", 100, m1);
_test(1, r1.get("music"), 100);
_test(2, r1.size, 1);

const m2 = new Map<string, number>([["gaming", 50]]);
const r2 = addChannel("sports", 200, m2);
_test(3, m2.has("sports"), false);
_test(4, r2.has("sports"), true);

const m3 = new Map<string, number>([["news", 10]]);
const r3 = addChannel("news", 999, m3);
_test(5, r3.get("news"), 999);

console.log('---------------------');
console.log(_pass + ' passed, ' + _fail + ' failed');

